uo;s 6 grids runs 1951 to 2025, and January to February came in under 90% of normal in 42 of those 75 years. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, June to July hit 132% of normal and November to December fell to 8%. Every grid had its driest year in 2011, with grid 15112 at 22% of normal. A preliminary estimate puts grid 15414 at 66.2 for August to September 2026.</p>"}
